{
  "title": "98: al-Bayyenah البينة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nلَمْ يَكُنِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ وَالْمُشْرِكِيْنَ مُنْفَكِّيْنَ حَتّٰى تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْبَيِّنَةُ ۙ‏(1)\nLAM YAKONIL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN AHLIL KETAABE WAL-MUSHREKEENA MUN-FAKKEENA HATTA TAA-TEYAHOMUL BAYYENATO.\nThe faithless from among the People of the Book and the polytheists were not set apart [from the community of the faithful] until the proof had come to them:\nرَسُوْلٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ يَتْلُوْا صُحُفًا مُّطَهَّرَةً ۙ‏(2)\nRASOOLUM MENAL LAAHE YATLOO SOHOFAM MOTAHHARATAN.\nan apostle from Allah reciting impeccable scriptures,\nفِيْهَا كُتُبٌ قَيِّمَةٌ ؕ‏(3)\nFEEHAA KOTOBUN QAYYEMAH.\nwherein are upright writings.\nوَمَا تَفَرَّقَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنَةُ ؕ‏(4)\nWA MAA TAFARRAQAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA ILLAA MIM BA’DE MAA JAA-AT-HOMUL BAYYENAH.\nThose who were given the Book did not divide except after the proof had come to them.\nوَمَاۤ اُمِرُوْۤا اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ ۙ حُنَفَآءَ وَيُقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَذٰلِكَ دِيْنُ الْقَيِّمَةِ ؕ‏(5)\nWA MAAA OMEROO ILLAA LE-YA’BODUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEENA, HONAFAAA-A WA YOQEEMUS SALAATA WA YOA-TUZ ZAKAATA WA ZAALEKA DEENUL QAYYEMAH.\nThough they were not commanded except to worship Allah, dedicating their faith to Him as men of pure faith, and to maintain the prayer and pay the zakat. That is the upright religion.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ وَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ شَرُّ الْبَرِيَّةِ ؕ‏(6)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN AHLIL KETAABE WAL-MUSHREKEENA FEE NAARE JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, OO-LAAA-EKA HUM SHARRUL BARIYYAH.\nIndeed the faithless from among the People of the Book and the polytheists will be in the fire of hell, to remain in it [forever]. It is they who are the worst of creatures.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ خَيْرُ الْبَرِيَّةِ ؕ‏(7)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE, OO-LAAA-EKA HUM KHAYRUL BARIYYAH.\nIndeed those who have faith and do righteous deeds—it is they who are the best of creatures.\nجَزَآؤُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ ؕ ذٰلِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِىَ رَبَّهٗ‏(8)\nJA-ZAAA-OHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM JANNAATO A’DNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA, RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WA RAZOO A’NH, ZAALEKA LEMAN KHASHEYA RABBAH.\nTheir reward, near their Lord, is the Gardens of Eden, with streams running in them, to remain in them forever. Allah is pleased with them, and they are pleased with Him. That is for those who fear their Lord.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Bayyenah (The Clear Evidence)\nThis Surah has 8 verses and it is a ‘Madani’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that if people knew the benefits of reciting this Surah, they would leave their work in order to learn it.\nIf a person recites this Surah at night, then Allah (s.w.t.) sends angels to protect the reciter and his faith is also secure. The angels seek forgiveness for him. The reward for reciting this Surah is equal to all those things on this Earth upon which the sun shines.\nWriting and drinking water of this Surah is beneficial for cure of ailments. Surah al-Bayyinah is also good for pregnant women and helps to ensure their safety and the safety of their babies. Reciting this Surah before eating food removes any ill effects of the foods."
}
